### Institutional application

Institutional Attrition

The progressive loss of institutional capacity, personnel, public confidence, procedural integrity, resources, or operational effectiveness.

Clerical Attrition

The gradual degradation of administrative continuity through personnel losses, documentary deficiencies, procedural interruptions, or accumulated administrative failures.

Autonomic Institutional Attrition

A proposed conceptual classification describing a self-perpetuating process through which an institution's own administrative mechanisms progressively diminish its operational capacity or integrity.

